  "body": "~~~js\r\nlet keepReading = true;\r\nlet reader;\r\n\r\nasync function readUntilClosed() {\r\n  while (port.readable && keepReading) {\r\n    reader = port.readable.pipeThrough(new TextDecoderStream()).getReader();\r\n    try {\r\n      while (true) {\r\n        const { value, done } = await reader.read();\r\n        if (done) {\r\n          // |reader| has been canceled.\r\n          break;\r\n        }\r\n        // Do something with |value|...\r\n      }\r\n    } catch (error) {\r\n      // Handle |error|...\r\n    } finally {\r\n      reader.releaseLock();\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  await port.close(); // <-- Uncaught (in promise) TypeError: Failed to execute 'close' on 'SerialPort': Cannot cancel a locked stream  at readUntilClosed\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst closed = readUntilClosed();\r\n\r\n// Sometime later...\r\nkeepReading = false;\r\nreader.cancel();\r\nawait closed;\r\n~~~\r\n\r\nI got an error at port.close(), port.readable still locked after reader.releaseLock(), \r\nhow to release lock in here. thanks.",
